What if the game was released in December of the prior season?

00:31:29.340 --> 00:31:31.380
They were just getting, like, real ready.

00:31:32.120 --> 00:31:38.200
You know, how Madden releases in, like, April or May or some shit or, like, I don't know.

00:31:38.600 --> 00:31:40.940
And the season doesn't start until September.

00:31:41.240 --> 00:31:43.200
It was like, oh, we're getting ready.

00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:47.060
We're releasing the game in December for whatever month you said.

00:31:47.300 --> 00:31:54.180
Yeah, for marketing purposes, I think that that's the right call is to release a year ahead.

00:31:54.640 --> 00:32:00.340
Yeah. But it is, there's, like, especially pre-internet, there's something weird about, like,

00:32:00.340 --> 00:32:03.940
if you're releasing a game with actual players and stuff and you release it before, like,

00:32:04.100 --> 00:32:09.080
the actual season so you don't even know, like, who was drafted and that stuff.

00:32:10.180 --> 00:32:19.200
You're right. We may not agree on how to name the game that you're playing based on the year that it's released in.

00:32:19.640 --> 00:32:20.720
I just said you were right.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:21.820
Oh, thank you.

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.300
Okay, so we do agree on that.

00:32:23.300 --> 00:32:32.700
And we'll have to agree on whether Little League Baseball Championship Series for the NES is on the Essential Games list.

00:32:33.120 --> 00:32:35.140
But also, we don't have to agree.

00:32:35.580 --> 00:32:38.720
Right, that's, like, one of the core rules of the Essential Games list.

00:32:42.220 --> 00:32:46.520
I think, presentationally, there is something nice here.

00:32:46.700 --> 00:32:50.940
I did enjoy my time, again, with a baseball NES game.

00:32:51.280 --> 00:32:56.580
But I've been enjoying my time with most of these NES baseball games outside of the ones that, like,

00:32:56.640 --> 00:33:00.880
the controls are just so horrendous that that's what I talk about for the entire episode.

00:33:01.100 --> 00:33:05.120
It's a good thing when we talk about these games now and we barely talk about the controls

00:33:05.120 --> 00:33:07.900
because that means that everything works as intended.

00:33:08.540 --> 00:33:11.980
I did bring up that thing about the swing, but to be honest, I kind of liked it.

00:33:12.180 --> 00:33:13.420
It wasn't a negative, actually.

00:33:13.580 --> 00:33:16.640
It was kind of cool that there was some motion to your swing.

00:33:16.820 --> 00:33:19.540
And I did feel like I was making good contact with the ball.

00:33:19.840 --> 00:33:23.120
And base running just worked the way I expected to now,

00:33:23.300 --> 00:33:26.260
where you can call back a runner or send a runner forward,

00:33:26.480 --> 00:33:29.720
depending on just pressing the right button in the right directional pad.

00:33:29.880 --> 00:33:32.500
It's like, great. Everything is happening.

00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:35.040
Pitching, it's like, I don't need to read the man.

00:33:35.120 --> 00:33:40.800
I just press a direction on the D-pad and I throw the ball and I'll just learn as I go

00:33:40.800 --> 00:33:43.060
what pitches which and what works for me.

00:33:43.400 --> 00:33:44.820
That's how baseball is played, right?

00:33:44.920 --> 00:33:47.780
You just kind of learn. You just kind of Jedi mind trick it in midair.

00:33:47.860 --> 00:33:50.000
Yeah, you just kind of learn what's going on.

00:33:50.460 --> 00:33:52.240
And that's what I did for this game.

00:33:52.380 --> 00:33:56.280
I played it pretty blind and I enjoyed my blind experience with it.

00:33:56.800 --> 00:34:00.500
The reason why I'm not going to put it on the essential games list, though,

00:34:01.460 --> 00:34:06.140
is mostly for the same reason that other NES baseball games haven't been on the essential games list,

00:34:06.180 --> 00:34:07.740
so we don't need to cover that ground too much.

00:34:07.820 --> 00:34:11.580
But just that it didn't leave me with a feeling of wanting to go back.

00:34:11.580 --> 00:34:16.960
If anything, it makes me want to go forward and play more advanced baseball video games.

00:34:16.960 --> 00:34:22.800
This is held back in time by its limitations and this is all it will ever be.

00:34:23.020 --> 00:34:25.440
So it's not going on the essential games list for me.

00:34:25.560 --> 00:34:26.440
But what about you, Sean?

00:34:27.920 --> 00:34:33.920
Yeah, this is a very slick and competent baseball game.

00:34:34.220 --> 00:34:37.100
I don't think we really talked about physics,

00:34:37.100 --> 00:34:45.100
but the ball just feels like very ball-like and like an actual object in this game.

00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:46.600
So I really appreciate that.

00:34:46.840 --> 00:34:50.420
I think compared to softball two weeks ago,

00:34:50.640 --> 00:34:55.320
I do, you know, as a holistic game full package,

00:34:55.320 --> 00:34:56.520
I do like this better.

00:34:57.940 --> 00:34:59.460
But for the same reasons,

00:34:59.640 --> 00:35:04.180
but also the cardinal sin of not showing me where my fielders are,

00:35:04.440 --> 00:35:05.520
can't really forgive that.

00:35:05.520 --> 00:35:06.920
But yeah, same reason.

00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:10.100
Like there's too much NES baseball.

00:35:10.920 --> 00:35:12.580
And as competent as it is,

00:35:12.640 --> 00:35:14.100
it doesn't like, I'm not going to,

00:35:14.700 --> 00:35:18.920
I'm not going to like think about this game again, probably.

00:35:20.080 --> 00:35:21.720
It's just, it was nice.

00:35:22.060 --> 00:35:23.260
So not essential.

00:35:24.040 --> 00:35:31.380
Joe. Inevitably, a day will come when Mike says to me on an episode,

00:35:31.620 --> 00:35:33.620
Joe, remember Little League Baseball?

00:35:33.620 --> 00:35:34.680
What did you think of that?

00:35:34.780 --> 00:35:35.660
Or something like that.

00:35:36.640 --> 00:35:38.560
And when that time comes,

00:35:38.600 --> 00:35:41.220
and I have obviously forgotten everything about this game,

00:35:41.360 --> 00:35:45.620
I want to record this to remind myself that this game was passable,

00:35:46.140 --> 00:35:48.020
but I'm definitely going to forget it.

00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:49.480
So not essential.

00:35:49.860 --> 00:35:50.920
Joe, you know,

00:35:51.020 --> 00:35:56.280
not for nothing, but it does prove that we can all agree on things when it comes to the essential game.

00:35:56.280 --> 00:35:57.520
We can. I just said we don't have to.

00:35:57.940 --> 00:35:59.040
We don't have to.

00:35:59.040 --> 00:36:02.440
Oh, I, uh, yeah, I'm trying to stipulate that we have to.

00:36:04.140 --> 00:36:05.620
Mike makes us all agree.

00:36:05.840 --> 00:36:06.760
Someone help. Send help.

00:36:08.180 --> 00:36:10.280
Uh, next week, what do we got?

00:36:10.500 --> 00:36:12.220
What do you think, what do you think next week is?

00:36:12.860 --> 00:36:14.160
Baseball, it's 40,

00:36:14.320 --> 00:36:15.800
4,000. No, no,

00:36:16.020 --> 00:36:17.120
it's every other game.

00:36:17.340 --> 00:36:18.340
What month is it?

00:36:19.660 --> 00:36:21.320
September? Is it September?

00:36:21.840 --> 00:36:22.700
Uh, yes, you're correct.

00:36:23.540 --> 00:36:24.600
Okay. That's pretty good.

00:36:24.740 --> 00:36:26.020
So you know what month it is.

00:36:26.440 --> 00:36:29.140
Joe, do you know what week it is of the year?

00:36:29.860 --> 00:36:34.140
It'll be, so it'll be the first week of September,

00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:37.880
which would be week number 42.

00:36:39.720 --> 00:36:43.140
That's wrong. That's gotta be wrong.

00:36:43.320 --> 00:36:44.460
That's way wrong. That's like November.

00:36:44.720 --> 00:36:45.620
Way more than September. Yeah,

00:36:45.700 --> 00:36:47.440
that's way more than September. Yeah, that's October.

00:36:47.780 --> 00:36:49.520
I don't know. Just in case people,

00:36:49.640 --> 00:36:50.680
just in case people do care,

00:36:50.960 --> 00:36:51.840
um, I'll say it now.

00:36:52.260 --> 00:36:53.800
Little League Baseball Championship Series

00:36:53.800 --> 00:36:55.720
